# Module-Owned Migrations

When changing DB schema in a module, add migrations **inside the module**, not in root `supabase/migrations`.

## Where to put migrations

- **Path**: `modules/<module-name>/supabase/migrations/`
- **Filename**: `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_plugin_<slug>.sql` (slug must start with `plugin_`)
- **Uniqueness**: No two modules may use the same migration basename

## Do / Don't

```bash
# ✅ Add migration in the module (plugin_ prefix required)
# modules/team/supabase/migrations/20260227120000_plugin_team_avatar.sql

# ❌ Do not add module schema in root; do not commit *_plugin_*.sql in supabase/migrations (gitignored)
```

## Commands

- **Aggregate** (run manually when needed): `pnpm migrations:aggregate`
- **Apply or push**: `pnpm supabase:migration:up` or `pnpm supabase:db:push` (run aggregate first if you added/changed module migrations)

Full details: [plugins.md](../../../docs/content/dev/plugins.md).
